# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Camea Mosaic Builder — PUBLISHED SUBSET ONLY.
#
# This working tree contains far more than it publishes: a ~35 GB read-only data
# mirror, the placement challenge, the hand-authored ground truth, notebooks, and
# the cross-session knowledge base. NONE of that is published.
#
# Strategy: DENY EVERYTHING, then allow back exactly the app and the engine it
# calls. A new top-level directory is invisible to git by default — that is the
# point. If you add something that SHOULD ship, allow it explicitly below.
#
# ⚠️ NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line. A comment
# after a pattern becomes PART OF THE PATTERN and silently matches nothing.
# Every comment here is on its own line, deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- 1. deny every top-level entry. This is what keeps data/ out, permanently.
/*

# --- 2. allow back the repo's own furniture
!/.gitignore
!/LICENSE
!/README.md
!/requirements.txt

# --- 3. the app
!/app/

# 138 MB of tissue screenshots, server logs, and EXPORTED GROUND TRUTH. Not published.
app/shots/

# not built yet
app/packaging/

# the build harness that produced the app — not part of the app
app/build_workflow.js
app/final_pass.js
app/PROMPT.md

# --- 4. the engine the app CALLS.
# Not a copy: the app imports these directly, so there is exactly one t33 and it
# cannot silently diverge from a fork.
!/analysis/
analysis/*
!analysis/mosaic/
!analysis/ground_truth/
!analysis/benchmark/

# ground_truth: the EXCLUSION RULE is code the app needs.
# The hand-authored ground-truth JSONs are unpublished research. They stay out.
analysis/ground_truth/*
!analysis/ground_truth/excluded.py

# benchmark: the scorer only. Its GT paths resolve to files that are not in this
# repo, which is fine — nothing reads them at module load.
analysis/benchmark/*
!analysis/benchmark/score.py

# --- 5. never, anywhere
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.camea.json
.playwright-mcp/
*.npz
*.npy
*.tif
*.tiff
